Error: Jet.RuntimeStringAsCheckedText: A runtime `String` can't be used as `Token`
  --> Tests/UI/sink_needs_checked_text.jet:28:10
    |
 28 |     send(text)
    |          ^^^^
 Why: `Token` is checked text, built only from a checked literal whose `{value}` holes its `CheckedText` impl encodes, so untrusted text can't change its meaning
 Fix: Write `Token{"..."}` with `{value}` holes, or use `Token.raw("…")` if you have audited the text
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.RuntimeStringAsCheckedText
